Welcome to this technical debate on feed element spacing balance in defocused systems. Our goal is to minimize dB loss while maintaining beamforming flexibility.

In defocused systems, feed elements at the border are more strongly defocused than those in the center. This can lead to significant gain loss when individual or multiple feed elements fail. We need to find a balance between feed element spacing and beamforming flexibility to mitigate this effect.

Can we start by discussing the trade-offs between feed element spacing, gain loss, and beamforming flexibility? What are the key considerations for designing a robust defocused system?

