In the link budget equations, the antenna efficiency affects parameters such as transmit power, noise temperature, and propagation losses. A lower efficiency means more power is lost as heat rather than being radiated, reducing the effective transmit power available for communication. This could lead to increased transmission power requirements or reduced coverage area. Furthermore, the noise temperature of the receiver increases with lower antenna efficiency, which in turn affects the signal-to-noise ratio (SNR) and the bit error rate.

